==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|s|u}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*soola}} (compare {{cog|et|sool}}, {{cog|vep|sol}}), from {{der|fi|ine-pro|*séh₂ls}}. Words of the same origin occur also in many other Uralic languages, for example {{cog|koi|сов}}, {{cog|udm|сылал}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈsuɔlɑ]|lang=fi}}
* {{hyphenation|suo|la|lang=fi}}
* {{rhymes|uolɑ|lang=fi}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia|lang=fi}}
{{head|fi|noun}}

# [[salt]] {{qualifier|common table salt, sodium chloride, NaCl}}
# salt {{qualifier|chemical compound formed from the reaction of an acid with a base}}
